    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
title: "Cancer Research: Cross-Literature Analysis and Multi-Modality Therapy Simulation"
type: software
version: "2026-04"
date-released: "2026-04-23"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/ELares/cancer_research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ELares/cancer_research"
abstract: >
  Open-source cancer research combining a census of the indexed cancer
  literature -- 5,187,265 articles, being 4,403,994 with MeSH indexing
  and 783,271 recovered by text match, carrying 10,509,470 typed entity
  relations -- with Monte Carlo biochemical simulations of nine cancer
  treatment arms: ferroptosis induction, photodynamic and sonodynamic
  therapy, ionizing radiation, checkpoint blockade, adoptive cell
  therapy, oncolytic virus, ablation and antibody-drug conjugates,
  across cell phenotypes, drug combinations, and tumor microenvironment
  features. The ferroptosis and physical-ROS arms carry the calibrated
  legs; the others are directional and are recorded as such. Claims are measured over articles the
  project did not select, using expert-assigned MeSH descriptors and
  NLM publication types rather than the project's own retrieval.
  Includes a reusable Rust simulation engine (ferroptosis-core) with
  Python bindings, a news source authentication pipeline, and a
  ~270-page book-format manuscript.
keywords:
  - cancer research
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - cross-literature analysis
  - ferroptosis
  - radiotherapy
  - immunotherapy
  - adoptive cell therapy
  - oncolytic virus
  - antibody-drug conjugate
  - tumor ablation
  - drug-tolerant persister cells
  - tumor microenvironment
  - sonodynamic therapy
  - open science
